Here's a basic HTML/JS setup for a colorful website that displays jokes and a "reveal punchline" button:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Joke Website</title>
    <style>
        body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: #f9f9f9; padding: 20px; }
        h1 { color: #3366cc; text-align: center; }
        .joke-container { border: 1px solid #ccc; margin-bottom: 20px; padding: 20px; }
        .punchline { display: none; }
        #reveal { background-color: #4CAF50; color: white; padding: 10px 20px; border: none; cursor: pointer; }
        #reveal:hover { background-color: #45a049; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<h1>My Joke Website</h1>

<div class="joke-container">
    <div id="setup">Why don't scientists trust atoms?</div>
    <button id="reveal">Push to reveal punchline</button>
    <div class="punchline" style="display: none;">They make up everything!</div>
</div>

<div class="joke-container">
    <div id="setup2">What do you call a fake noodle?</div>
    <button id="reveal2">Push to reveal punchline</button>
    <div class="punchline" style="display: none;">An impasta!</div>
</div>

<script>
    document.getElementById('reveal').addEventListener('click', function() {
        document.querySelector('.punchline').style.display = 'block';
    });

    document.getElementById('reveal2').addEventListener('click', function() {
        document.querySelector('#setup2 ~ .punchline').style.display = 'block';
    });
</script>

</body>
</html>
```

