Here's some basic HTML and JavaScript to create an interactive joke website with a "push to reveal punchline" feature:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>My Joke Website</title>
<style>
  body {
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    background-color: #f4f4f4;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 50px;
    color: #333;
  }
  .joke-container {
    border: 2px solid #000;
    padding: 50px;
    max-width: 600px;
    margin: auto;
  }
  .joke-container h1 {
    color: #000;
  }
  .joke-container p {
    text-align: center;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  button {
    cursor: pointer;
    padding: 10px 20px;
    border: none;
    color: white;
    background-color: green;
    font-size: 1em;
  }
  button:hover {
    background-color: darkgreen;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="joke-container">
  <h1>My Joke Website</h1>
  <p id="joke">[Funny Joke]</p>
  <button id="revealButton">Push to reveal punchline</button>
  <script>
    document.getElementById('revealButton').addEventListener('click', function() {
      var joke = document.getElementById('joke');
      if (joke.innerHTML === '[Funny Joke]') {
        joke.innerHTML = 'Why don\'t scientists trust atoms? Because they make up everything!';
      } else {
        joke.innerHTML = '[Funny Joke]';
      }
    });
  </script>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

This code will create a website with a simple design. When the button is clicked, it replaces the placeholder `[Funny Joke]` with a real joke. The joke content is hardcoded for demonstration purposes but can be changed or dynamically loaded from an API based on your needs.
